review_comments:
This wraps the PolyglotEngineException twice when it is rethrown.
It also exposes a PolyglotEngineException to the user, which should never happen. PolyglotEngineException is intended to always be unwrapped before shown to the outside world.

And a different exception other than IllegalStateException should be handled correctly. This means:

1) If the callback comes from the embedder any exception other than an IllegalStateException must be wrapped as HostException.
2) If the callback comes from a language any AbstractTruffleException must be rethrown.

A correct implementation would look like this:
```
void rethrow(PolyglotContextImpl context) {
    RuntimeException t;
    assert !Thread.holdsLock(context) : "Only rethrow without holding internal lock";
    Consumer<RuntimeException> consumer = context.config.onDeniedThreadAccess;
    IllegalStateException ex = new IllegalStateException(t.getMessage());
    if (consumer != null) {
        try {
          consumer.accept(ex);
        } catch (IllegalStateException e) {
            throw new PolyglotEngineException(e);
        } catch (Throwable another) {
            if (context.parent != null) { // inner context
                // inner context. no wrapping needed
                throw another;
            } else {
                // embedder context
                throw PolyglotImpl.hostToGuestException(context.engine, another);
            }
        }
    } else {
        throw new PolyglotEngineException(ex);
    }
}
```
But I think we should do the API differently to simplify serialization.
